      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Executive summary",
      "pageStart": 11,
      "pageEnd": 19,
      "target": "../sections/sec-002-executive-summary.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Executive summary\nIntroduction\nIn 2016, at the start of the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) era, pregnancy-related preventable morbidity \nand mortality remains unacceptably high. While substantial progress has been made, countries need to \nconsolidate and increase these advances, and to expand their agendas to go beyond survival, with a view to \nmaximizing the health and potential of their populations.\nThe World Health Organization (WHO) envisions a world where every pregnant woman and newborn receives \nquality care throughout the pregnancy, childbirth and the postnatal period. Within the",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Executive summary of the 2016 WHO antenatal care (ANC) guideline. Defines a 'positive pregnancy experience' around four pillars (maintaining physical and sociocultural normality, maintaining a healthy pregnancy for mother and baby, effective transition to positive labour and birth, and achieving positive motherhood), outlines the GRADE, GRADE-CERQual, and DECIDE Evidence-to-Decision (EtD) methods used across three GDG technical consultations in 2015–2016, explains the shift from the 4-visit focused ANC (FANC) model to a minimum of eight ANC contacts, and presents Table 1 summarizing all 49 recommendations (39 newly formulated by the GDG and 10 integrated from existing WHO guidelines) across five intervention categories: A. Nutritional interventions, B. Maternal and fetal assessment, C. Preventive measures, D. Interventions for common physiological symptoms, and E. Health systems interventions.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-28"
