    {
      "id": "library/9789241549912-eng/blocks/prose-sec-004",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Methods",
      "pageStart": 22,
      "pageEnd": 31,
      "target": "../sections/sec-004-2-methods.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "2. Methods\nThe guideline was developed in accordance with \nthe methods described in the WHO handbook for \nguideline development (14). In summary, the process \nincluded: identification of priority questions and \noutcomes, retrieval of evidence, assessment \nand synthesis of the evidence, formulation \nof recommendations, and planning for the \nimplementation, dissemination, impact evaluation \nand updating of the guideline.\n2.1 WHO Steering Group\nThe WHO Steering Group that guided the entire \nguideline development process comprised WHO \nstaff members from the Department of Reproductive \nHealth and",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Chapter 2 (Methods) detailing the governance and methodological processes used to develop the 2016 WHO ANC guideline in accordance with the 2014 WHO handbook for guideline development. Describes the composition and roles of the WHO Steering Group (RHR, MCA, NHD, plus HIV, Malaria, TB, and Mental Health/Substance Abuse units), the 20-member Guideline Development Group (GDG), the 6-member External Review Group (ERG), and the Technical Working Group (TWG); the 2014 scoping exercise and PICO prioritization; cross-checking and integration of 21 GRC-approved WHO guidelines; the five evidence work streams summarized in Box 2 (quantitative intervention and DTA reviews, qualitative syntheses on women's and providers' views, and FANC country case studies in Argentina, Kenya, Thailand, and the United Republic of Tanzania); quality assessment via GRADE and GRADE-CERQual; the DECIDE Evidence-to-Decision (EtD) framework across effects, values, resources, equity, acceptability, and feasibility; recommendation classification ('Recommended', 'Not recommended', and 'Context-specific recommendation' in research or specific contexts); consensus decision-making; declaration of interest management; and document peer review.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-28"
