    {
      "id": "library/9789241549912-eng/blocks/prose-sec-007",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "B. Maternal and fetal assessment",
      "pageStart": 58,
      "pageEnd": 81,
      "target": "../sections/sec-007-b-maternal-and-fetal-assessment.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "B. Maternal and fetal assessment\nB.1: Maternal assessment\nBackground\nHypertensive disorders of pregnancy are important \ncauses of maternal and perinatal morbidity and \nmortality, with approximately a quarter of maternal \ndeaths and near misses estimated to be due to pre-\neclampsia and eclampsia (9). Antenatal screening \nfor pre-eclampsia is an essential part of good ANC. \nIt is routinely performed by measuring maternal \nblood pressure and checking for proteinuria at each \nANC contact and, upon detection of pre-eclampsia, \nspecific management is required to prevent eclampsia \nand other poor mat",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Chapter 3, Section B (Maternal and fetal assessment), covering evidence syntheses, EtD judgements, and clinical remarks for maternal assessments B.1.1–B.1.8 and fetal assessments B.2.1–B.2.5. Maternal assessments include B.1.1 full blood count testing or on-site haemoglobinometer over haemoglobin colour scale for diagnosing anaemia in pregnancy (context-specific), B.1.2 midstream urine culture or on-site Gram stain over dipstick tests for diagnosing asymptomatic bacteriuria (context-specific), B.1.3 clinical enquiry about intimate partner violence (IPV) at ANC visits when minimum support and referral requirements are met (context-specific, with Box 3 listing IPV signs/conditions), B.1.4 diagnostic criteria and 75 g OGTT thresholds for hyperglycaemia/gestational diabetes mellitus (GDM) in pregnancy (recommended, integrated from 2013 WHO guideline), B.1.5 routine enquiry on tobacco use and second-hand smoke exposure at every ANC visit (recommended, integrated), B.1.6 routine enquiry on alcohol and substance use at every ANC visit (recommended, integrated), B.1.7 provider-initiated HIV testing and counselling (PITC) in high-prevalence and low-prevalence settings integrated with syphilis and other key tests (recommended/context-specific, integrated), and B.1.8 systematic screening for active tuberculosis where TB prevalence is ≥100/100,000 (context-specific, integrated). Fetal assessments include B.2.1 daily fetal movement counting (context-specific research), B.2.2 symphysis-fundal height (SFH) measurement versus clinical abdominal palpation (context-specific), B.2.3 routine antenatal cardiotocography (not recommended), B.2.4 one early ultrasound scan before 24 weeks of gestation (recommended), and B.2.5 routine Doppler ultrasound of fetal blood vessels (not recommended).",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-28"
