    {
      "id": "library/9789241549912-eng/blocks/prose-sec-010",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Research implications",
      "pageStart": 136,
      "pageEnd": 139,
      "target": "../sections/sec-010-5-research-implications.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "During the guideline development process, the \nGuideline Development Group (GDG) identified \nimportant knowledge gaps that need to be addressed \nthrough primary research. The certainty of evidence \nwas rated as “low” or “very low” for a number of \ninterventions evaluated. According to GRADE \nmethodology (15), this implies that further research \non interventions with “low” or “very low” certainty \nevidence for important outcomes is likely to have \nan impact on future certainty and subsequent \nrecommendations related to these interventions. The \nGDG identified knowledge gaps based on this concep",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Chapter 5 (Research implications—continuation of Box 7) and Chapter 6, Section 6.1 (Guideline dissemination). Completes Box 7's priority research questions across Section B (on-site anaemia and ASB diagnostics, IPV enquiry, early ultrasound before 24 weeks in LMICs, and Doppler ultrasound), Section C (short vs 7-day ASB antibiotics, RUTI prophylaxis, anti-D immunoglobulin in LMICs, and malaria/HIV interactions), Section D (physiological symptoms), and Section E (electronic vs paper woman-held notes, MLCC scale-up, group ANC trials, community mobilization, and impact of the 8-contact schedule). Section 6.1 outlines dissemination in all six UN languages through WHO regional/country offices, the WHO Reproductive Health Library (RHL), evidence briefs co-produced with USAID, FIGO, and ICM, an interactive web-based guideline platform, HRP News, and the OptimizeMNH database.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
